INT. WEDDING RECEPTION - RIVERBOAT BALLROOM - NIGHT

Paper lanterns sway on a gilded deck. A band plays under strung lights. Champagne flutes shiver on a long white table.

Four guests huddle near the cake: the bride's sister IMANI LOCKHART-DEVEREUX (30s, bridesmaid, sage-green dress), her ex-boyfriend FERNANDO CASTELLANOS (30s, best man, too-tight tie), his mother DONA GLORIA CASTELLANOS (60s, black lace, fan in hand), and an elderly cousin, UNCLE ABEL (70s, braces, cane).

Imani and Fernando stand a pace apart, the way people do when they have both rehearsed a speech and forgotten it.

IMANI
You look well.

FERNANDO
You look... green.

IMANI
It's sage.

Gloria snaps her fan open. Abel leans heavily on his cane and squints at the cake. Imani and Fernando both reach for the same champagne flute, their fingers meeting on the stem. They freeze. The band hits a slow chord.

FERNANDO
After you.

IMANI
After you.

Gloria and Abel exchange a glance, shuffle to opposite sides of the cake, and, as if on cue, begin to cut it, passing the knife between them with elaborate ceremony.

FADE OUT.
